{"id": 50, "ts": 1779611785.2276487, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "Having reviewed the current evidence, I see that Candidate\u202fA lacks any documented proof of operational reliability and shows limited openness to feedback, both critical for long\u2011distance operations. Candidate\u202fC, on the other hand, demonstrably meets the core safety\u2011critical criteria: 100\u202f% reliability, calmness under pressure, rapid correct decision\u2011making, solid technical competence, and excellent attention to detail, plus a positive crew atmosphere. While we still have no direct observations of C\u2019s responsibility in cockpit contexts or his adaptability to feedback, these gaps are less severe than the unanswered reliability and feedback concerns for A and the teamwork deficits for B and D. Therefore, I update my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**. We should continue to seek any additional observations on C\u2019s responsibility and adaptability, and on D\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation and communication, to confirm this choice."}
